WEBVTT

00:36:28.538 --> 00:36:31.788
we didn't actually do as good of a job
on the alignment work as we thought.

00:36:32.163 --> 00:36:36.663
And this sort of child of
humanity kind of acts in

00:36:36.663 --> 00:36:37.954
a very different way than we think.

00:36:38.371 --> 00:36:42.746
A framework that I find useful is to sort
of think about like a two by two matrix,

00:36:42.746 --> 00:36:47.704
which is short timelines to ajai
and long timelines to ajai and

00:36:47.704 --> 00:36:50.996
a slow take off and a fast take
off on the other axis.

00:36:51.663 --> 00:36:56.913
And in the short timelines,
fast take off quadrant,

00:36:57.204 --> 00:36:58.413
which is not where I think
we're going to be.

00:36:58.746 --> 00:37:01.496
But if we get there, I think there's
a lot of scenarios in